[
  {"id": "dec-pi-enu", "name": "π⁺ → e⁺ ν_e", "difficulty": 3, "explanation": "The diagram is identical to π⁺ → μ⁺ν_μ with the lepton replaced, yet the rate is about 8 000 times smaller. The π⁺ has spin 0 and the V−A current produces the lepton pair with fixed helicities, so the rate is proportional to the lepton mass squared. This helicity suppression is invisible in the diagram.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [2, 0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "l": [3, -0.6], "n": [3, 0.6]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "u"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v1", "dbar"], ["lep", "out", "l", "v2", "e+"], ["nu", "out", "n", "v2", "nu_e"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W+"]], "hadrons": [["P", "pi+", "in", ["a", "b"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["helicity"], "br": 0.000123, "brText": "(1.230 ± 0.004) × 10⁻⁴", "compareWith": "dec-pi-munu"}, "hideSets": [["lep"], ["nu"], ["W"], ["lep", "W"]]},
  {"id": "dec-k-enu", "name": "K⁺ → e⁺ ν_e", "difficulty": 3, "explanation": "This has the same diagram as K⁺ → μ⁺ν_μ, but the electron mass is so small that the helicity-suppressed rate is only about 2.5 × 10⁻⁵ of the muon mode. The spin-0 kaon must produce the lepton pair with fixed helicities, and the rate scales with the lepton mass squared. Helicity suppression is invisible in the diagram.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [2, 0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "l": [3, -0.6], "n": [3, 0.6]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "u"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v1", "sbar"], ["lep", "out", "l", "v2", "e+"], ["nu", "out", "n", "v2", "nu_e"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W+"]], "hadrons": [["P", "K+", "in", ["a", "b"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["helicity"], "br": 1.582e-05, "brText": "(1.582 ± 0.007) × 10⁻⁵", "compareWith": "dec-k-munu"}, "hideSets": [["lep"], ["nu"], ["W"], ["lep", "W"]]},
  {"id": "dec-d0-pipi", "name": "D⁰ → π⁺ π⁻", "difficulty": 5, "explanation": "The charm quark decays to d instead of s, so the vertex uses |V_cd| of about 0.22 instead of |V_cs| of about 0.97. This singly Cabibbo-suppressed decay has a rate of only a few percent of D⁰ → K⁻π⁺.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.4], "v2": [2, -1.0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "w1": [3, -1.5], "w2": [3, -1.0], "s1": [3, -0.25], "s2": [3, 0.25]}, "legs": [["dq", "in", "a", "v1", "c"], ["new", "out", "s1", "v1", "d"], ["p1", "out", "w1", "v2", "u"], ["p2", "out", "w2", "v2", "dbar"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "s2", "ubar"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W+"]], "hadrons": [["P", "D0", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Mw", "pi+", "out", ["w1", "w2"]], ["Ms", "pi-", "out", ["s1", "s2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["cabibbo-single"], "br": 0.001453, "brText": "(1.453 ± 0.024) × 10⁻³", "compareWith": "dec-d0-kpi"}, "hideSets": [["W"]]},
  {"id": "dec-d0-kpi-dcs", "name": "D⁰ → K⁺ π⁻", "difficulty": 5, "explanation": "Both weak vertices pay a Cabibbo factor: c → d uses |V_cd| and the W⁺ → u s̄ uses |V_us|. This doubly Cabibbo-suppressed decay has a rate of only about 0.4 % of D⁰ → K⁻π⁺. In practice D⁰–D̄⁰ mixing can feed the same final state.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.4], "v2": [2, -1.0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "w1": [3, -1.5], "w2": [3, -1.0], "s1": [3, -0.25], "s2": [3, 0.25]}, "legs": [["dq", "in", "a", "v1", "c"], ["new", "out", "s1", "v1", "d"], ["p1", "out", "w1", "v2", "u"], ["p2", "out", "w2", "v2", "sbar"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "s2", "ubar"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W+"]], "hadrons": [["P", "D0", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Mw", "K+", "out", ["w1", "w2"]], ["Ms", "pi-", "out", ["s1", "s2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["cabibbo-double"], "br": 0.00015, "brText": "(1.50 ± 0.07) × 10⁻⁴", "compareWith": "dec-d0-kpi"}, "hideSets": [["W"]]},
  {"id": "dec-b0bar-pipi", "name": "B̄⁰ → π⁺ π⁻", "difficulty": 5, "explanation": "The b quark decays to u rather than c, which costs |V_ub|/|V_cb|, about 0.09, in amplitude. As a result B̄⁰ → π⁺π⁻ is roughly 500 times rarer than B̄⁰ → D⁺π⁻. Penguin loops add a competing amplitude.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.4], "v2": [2, -1.0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "w1": [3, -1.5], "w2": [3, -1.0], "s1": [3, -0.25], "s2": [3, 0.25]}, "legs": [["dq", "in", "a", "v1", "b"], ["new", "out", "s1", "v1", "u"], ["p1", "out", "w1", "v2", "d"], ["p2", "out", "w2", "v2", "ubar"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "s2", "dbar"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W-"]], "hadrons": [["P", "B0bar", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Mw", "pi-", "out", ["w1", "w2"]], ["Ms", "pi+", "out", ["s1", "s2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["ckm-b-u"], "br": 5.37e-06, "brText": "(5.37 ± 0.20) × 10⁻⁶ (CP conjugate of the PDG B⁰ mode)", "compareWith": "dec-b0bar-dpi"}, "hideSets": [["W"]]},
  {"id": "dec-b0bar-d0pi0", "name": "B̄⁰ → D⁰ π⁰", "difficulty": 5, "explanation": "The W⁻ is emitted inside the diagram: its ū must go into the D⁰ and its d into the π⁰, together with the c quark and the spectator. The colors of those quark pairs must match, which suppresses the amplitude by roughly a factor of 1/3. The rate is about a tenth of B̄⁰ → D⁺π⁻.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.6], "v2": [2, -0.1]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "c1": [3, -1.0], "c2": [3, -0.5], "n1": [3, 0.0], "n2": [3, 0.5]}, "legs": [["dq", "in", "a", "v1", "b"], ["new", "out", "c1", "v1", "c"], ["p1", "out", "c2", "v2", "ubar"], ["p2", "out", "n1", "v2", "d"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "n2", "dbar"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W-"]], "hadrons": [["P", "B0bar", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Mc", "D0", "out", ["c1", "c2"]], ["Mn", "pi0", "out", ["n1", "n2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["color"], "br": 0.000267, "brText": "(2.67 ± 0.09) × 10⁻⁴ (CP conjugate of the PDG B⁰ mode)", "compareWith": "dec-b0bar-dpi"}, "hideSets": [["W"], ["P"], ["W", "P"]]},
  {"id": "dec-b0-jpsiks", "name": "B⁰ → J/ψ K_S", "difficulty": 5, "explanation": "The W⁺ from b̄ → c̄ W⁺ becomes c s̄, and the c quark must pair with the c̄ from the b̄ decay to make the J/ψ. Matching colors between the two quark pairs costs the color-suppression factor, the same topology as B̄⁰ → D⁰π⁰. The decay is famous because B⁰ and B̄⁰ both reach this final state, which makes CP violation measurable.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.6], "v2": [2, -0.1]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "c1": [3, -1.0], "c2": [3, -0.5], "n1": [3, 0.0], "n2": [3, 0.5]}, "legs": [["dq", "in", "a", "v1", "bbar"], ["new", "out", "c1", "v1", "cbar"], ["p1", "out", "c2", "v2", "c"], ["p2", "out", "n1", "v2", "sbar"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "n2", "d"]], "edges": [["W", "v1", "v2", "W+"]], "hadrons": [["P", "B0", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Mc", "jpsi", "out", ["c1", "c2"]], ["Mn", "K_S", "out", ["n1", "n2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["color"], "br": 0.0004455, "brText": "≈ 4.5 × 10⁻⁴ (half of B(B⁰ → J/ψ K⁰) = (8.91 ± 0.21) × 10⁻⁴)", "compareWith": "dec-b0-dpi"}, "hideSets": [["W"], ["P"], ["W", "P"]]},
  {"id": "dec-phi-3pi", "name": "φ → π⁺ π⁻ π⁰", "difficulty": 6, "explanation": "The s s̄ pair of the φ has no quark in common with the pions, so it must annihilate into three gluons first (the OZI rule). Three gluons are needed because C-parity forbids two. This suppresses φ → 3π relative to φ → K⁺K⁻, where the strange quarks flow straight into the kaons.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.3], "v2": [2, 0], "v3": [3, 0.3], "w1": [2.2, -1.6], "w2": [5, 0.6], "w3": [4, 1.3]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.3], "b": [0, 0.3], "o1": [6, -2.5], "o2": [6, -2.0], "o3": [6, -0.9], "o4": [6, -0.4], "o5": [6, 0.3], "o6": [6, 0.8]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "s"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v3", "sbar"], ["u1", "out", "o1", "w1", "u"], ["u1b", "out", "o2", "w1", "ubar"], ["u3", "out", "o3", "w3", "u"], ["d2b", "out", "o4", "w2", "dbar"], ["d2", "out", "o5", "w2", "d"], ["u3b", "out", "o6", "w3", "ubar"]], "edges": [["s1", "v1", "v2", "s"], ["s2", "v2", "v3", "s"], ["gA", "v1", "w1", "g"], ["gB", "v2", "w3", "g"], ["gC", "v3", "w2", "g"]], "hadrons": [["P", "phi", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Pi0", "pi0", "out", ["o1", "o2"]], ["PiP", "pi+", "out", ["o3", "o4"]], ["PiM", "pi-", "out", ["o5", "o6"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "strong", "reasons": ["ozi"], "br": 0.149, "brText": "(14.9 ± 0.4) %", "compareWith": "dec-phi-kk"}, "hideSets": [["s1"], ["s2"], ["gA"], ["gB"]]},
  {"id": "dec-jpsi-3pi", "name": "J/ψ → π⁺ π⁻ π⁰", "difficulty": 6, "explanation": "The c c̄ pair in the J/ψ has no quark in common with the pions, so it must annihilate into three gluons (the OZI rule) before light quarks appear. The J/ψ lies below the D D̄ threshold, so no OZI-allowed decay exists and its width is only about 93 keV. A virtual photon also contributes to this final state.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.3], "v2": [2, 0], "v3": [3, 0.3], "w1": [2.2, -1.6], "w2": [5, 0.6], "w3": [4, 1.3]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.3], "b": [0, 0.3], "o1": [6, -2.5], "o2": [6, -2.0], "o3": [6, -0.9], "o4": [6, -0.4], "o5": [6, 0.3], "o6": [6, 0.8]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "c"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v3", "cbar"], ["u1", "out", "o1", "w1", "u"], ["u1b", "out", "o2", "w1", "ubar"], ["u3", "out", "o3", "w3", "u"], ["d2b", "out", "o4", "w2", "dbar"], ["d2", "out", "o5", "w2", "d"], ["u3b", "out", "o6", "w3", "ubar"]], "edges": [["s1", "v1", "v2", "c"], ["s2", "v2", "v3", "c"], ["gA", "v1", "w1", "g"], ["gB", "v2", "w3", "g"], ["gC", "v3", "w2", "g"]], "hadrons": [["P", "jpsi", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Pi0", "pi0", "out", ["o1", "o2"]], ["PiP", "pi+", "out", ["o3", "o4"]], ["PiM", "pi-", "out", ["o5", "o6"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "strong", "reasons": ["ozi"], "br": 0.02, "brText": "(2.00 ± 0.07) %", "compareWith": "dec-jpsi-mumu"}, "hideSets": [["s1"], ["s2"], ["gA"], ["gB"]]},
  {"id": "dec-omega-pipi", "name": "ω → π⁺ π⁻", "difficulty": 4, "explanation": "The quark diagram looks exactly like ρ⁰ → π⁺π⁻, but the ω has G-parity −1 and two pions have G-parity +1, so the strong interaction cannot make this decay. It proceeds only through isospin breaking, mainly ρ–ω mixing, and is about 60 times rarer than ω → π⁺π⁻π⁰. G-parity violation is invisible in the diagram.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, -0.25], "v2": [2, 0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, -0.25], "b": [0, 0.25], "o1a": [3, -1.2], "o1b": [3, -0.7], "o2a": [3, 0.7], "o2b": [3, 1.2]}, "legs": [["q1", "in", "a", "v1", "u"], ["q1o", "out", "o1a", "v1", "u"], ["pb", "out", "o1b", "v2", "dbar"], ["pq", "out", "o2a", "v2", "d"]], "spectators": [["q2", "b", "o2b", "ubar"]], "edges": [["glu", "v1", "v2", "g"]], "hadrons": [["P", "omega", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["M1", "pi+", "out", ["o1a", "o1b"]], ["M2", "pi-", "out", ["o2a", "o2b"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "em", "reasons": ["isospin"], "br": 0.0153, "brText": "(1.53 ± 0.12) %", "compareWith": "dec-omega-3pi"}, "hideSets": [["glu"], ["M1"], ["M2"], ["glu", "M1"]]},
  {"id": "dec-kl-mumu", "name": "K_L → μ⁺ μ⁻", "difficulty": 7, "explanation": "A flavor-changing neutral transition d s̄ → μ⁺μ⁻ cannot happen at tree level, so this short-distance picture goes through a W box with a u, c or t quark inside. The GIM mechanism makes the up-type contributions nearly cancel, and the final state is helicity suppressed as well. The measured rate is dominated by a long-distance two-photon route, and the box is only a small part of it.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [1, 2], "v3": [3, 0], "v4": [3, 2]}, "externals": {"a": [0, 0], "b": [0, 2], "m": [4, -0.4], "n": [4, 2.4]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "d"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v2", "sbar"], ["mum", "out", "m", "v3", "mu-"], ["mup", "out", "n", "v4", "mu+"]], "edges": [["U", "v1", "v2", "u"], ["Wa", "v1", "v3", "W-"], ["Wb", "v2", "v4", "W+"], ["N", "v4", "v3", "nu_mu"]], "hadrons": [["P", "K_L", "in", ["a", "b"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["loop-gim", "helicity"], "br": 6.84e-09, "brText": "(6.84 ± 0.11) × 10⁻⁹", "compareWith": "dec-kl-pienu"}, "hideSets": [["mum"], ["mup"], ["U"], ["Wa"]]},
  {"id": "dec-bs-mumu", "name": "B_s → μ⁺ μ⁻", "difficulty": 7, "explanation": "The B_s (s b̄) cannot annihilate into μ⁺μ⁻ at tree level, so it goes through a W box with a top quark inside; Z penguins contribute as well. The loop and helicity suppression push the rate down to about 3 × 10⁻⁹. The Standard Model prediction is precise, so a deviation would signal new physics.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [1, 2], "v3": [3, 0], "v4": [3, 2]}, "externals": {"a": [0, 0], "b": [0, 2], "m": [4, -0.4], "n": [4, 2.4]}, "legs": [["q", "in", "a", "v1", "s"], ["qb", "in", "b", "v2", "bbar"], ["mum", "out", "m", "v3", "mu-"], ["mup", "out", "n", "v4", "mu+"]], "edges": [["U", "v1", "v2", "t"], ["Wa", "v1", "v3", "W-"], ["Wb", "v2", "v4", "W+"], ["N", "v4", "v3", "nu_mu"]], "hadrons": [["P", "Bs", "in", ["a", "b"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["loop-gim", "helicity"], "br": 3.34e-09, "brText": "(3.34 ± 0.27) × 10⁻⁹", "compareWith": "dec-bs-dspi"}, "hideSets": [["mum"], ["mup"], ["U"], ["Wa"]]},
  {"id": "dec-k-pinunu", "name": "K⁺ → π⁺ ν ν̄", "difficulty": 7, "explanation": "The s̄ → d̄ transition with a neutral ν ν̄ pair cannot happen at tree level, so it goes through a loop (a box or a Z penguin) with up-type quarks. The GIM mechanism and the small CKM factor |V_td| make the rate tiny, about 10⁻¹⁰. Because the Standard Model prediction is clean, this decay is a sensitive probe of new physics.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [1, 2], "v3": [3, 0], "v4": [3, 2]}, "externals": {"a": [0, 1.0], "b": [0, 1.6], "n1": [4, -0.6], "n2": [4, 2.6], "p1": [4, 3.2], "p2": [4, 3.8]}, "legs": [["sb", "in", "a", "v1", "sbar"], ["dbar", "out", "p1", "v2", "dbar"], ["nu", "out", "n1", "v3", "nu_e"], ["nub", "out", "n2", "v4", "anti_nu_e"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "p2", "u"]], "edges": [["U", "v2", "v1", "u"], ["Wa", "v1", "v3", "W+"], ["Wb", "v2", "v4", "W-"], ["L", "v4", "v3", "e-"]], "hadrons": [["K", "K+", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["Pi", "pi+", "out", ["p1", "p2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["loop-gim"], "br": 1.14e-10, "brText": "(1.14 +0.40 −0.33) × 10⁻¹⁰", "compareWith": "dec-k-pi0enu"}, "hideSets": [["nu"], ["nub"], ["U"], ["Wa"]]},
  {"id": "dec-b0bar-kstgamma", "name": "B̄⁰ → K̄*⁰ γ", "difficulty": 7, "explanation": "The b → s transition is forbidden at tree level, so it goes through a loop with a W and a top quark (a penguin) that radiates the photon. The loop and the GIM mechanism give a rate of order 10⁻⁵, about 1/60 of B̄⁰ → D⁺π⁻.", "vertices": {"v1": [1, 0], "v2": [2, -0.9], "v3": [3, 0]}, "externals": {"a": [0, 0], "b": [0, 1.2], "ph": [4, -2.2], "o1": [4, 0], "o2": [4, 1.2]}, "legs": [["b", "in", "a", "v1", "b"], ["s", "out", "o1", "v3", "s"], ["ph", "out", "ph", "v2", "gamma"]], "spectators": [["sp", "b", "o2", "dbar"]], "edges": [["t1", "v1", "v2", "t"], ["t2", "v2", "v3", "t"], ["W", "v1", "v3", "W-", 0.4]], "hadrons": [["P", "B0bar", "in", ["a", "b"]], ["K", "Kst0bar", "out", ["o1", "o2"]]], "decay": {"category": "suppressed", "interaction": "weak", "reasons": ["loop-gim"], "br": 4.18e-05, "brText": "(4.18 ± 0.25) × 10⁻⁵ (CP conjugate of the PDG B⁰ mode)", "compareWith": "dec-b0bar-dpi"}, "hideSets": [["t1"], ["t2"], ["W"], ["t1", "t2"]]}
]
